        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This updates the IDL unsigned integer properties of RTCTransportStats to say that the value is a \"<code class=\"notranslate\">non-negative</code> integer\" rather than a positive integer. The difference being that 0 is not positive (or negative).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">There are probably many other cases of this error in web API, sadly some added by me.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is an in-passing fix related to <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5170080646\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45185\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/45185/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45185\">#45185</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45296",
            "title": "RTCTransportStats integer props are non-negative",
            "date_modified": "2026-08-24T07:08:22.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-08-24T07:06:38.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/189964965?u=5e030a50f854f5d4d5c0c9e3e0d2599fe830e4f2&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">The interactive example on <code class=\"notranslate\">TypedArray.prototype.findLast</code> calls <code class=\"notranslate\">find()</code> rather than <code class=\"notranslate\">findLast()</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-js notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"const int8 = new Int8Array([10, 0, -10, 20, -30, 40, 50]);\nconsole.log(int8.find(isNegative));\n// Expected output: -30\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">const</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">int8</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">new</span> <span class=\"pl-v\">Int8Array</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">[</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">10</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">0</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">-</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">10</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">20</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">-</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">30</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">40</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">50</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">]</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span>\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">console</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-en\">log</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-s1\">int8</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-en\">find</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-s1\">isNegative</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span>\n<span class=\"pl-c\">// Expected output: -30</span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">find()</code> returns the <em>first</em> negative element, <code class=\"notranslate\">-10</code>. The documented output <code class=\"notranslate\">-30</code> is the <em>last</em> one, which is what <code class=\"notranslate\">findLast()</code> returns. So the example both contradicts its own stated output and demonstrates the wrong method on the page that documents <code class=\"notranslate\">findLast</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Verified in Node:</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"find     : -10\nfindLast : -30\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">find     : -10\nfindLast : -30\n</code></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Changing the call to <code class=\"notranslate\">findLast()</code> makes the example produce the documented <code class=\"notranslate\">-30</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I checked the sibling pages and they are all correct: <code class=\"notranslate\">typedarray/findLastIndex</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">typedarray/findIndex</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">typedarray/find</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">array/findLast</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">array/findLastIndex</code> each call their own method. This is the only page with the mismatch.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Found by executing every <code class=\"notranslate\">js interactive-example</code> block under <code class=\"notranslate\">files/en-us/web/javascript</code> that carries an <code class=\"notranslate\">// Expected output:</code> comment and comparing the actual scalar output against the documented one: 467 blocks ran, and this was the single value mismatch.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45291",
            "title": "fix(javascript): call findLast in the TypedArray.findLast example",
            "date_modified": "2026-08-23T14:19:30.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-08-23T14:17:46.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "rajanpanth",
                "url": "https://github.com/rajanpanth"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/185269030?u=1fc22565ccf4566b6f734fabaa87e03d9a31cfe4&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Restructures the <code class=\"notranslate\">&amp; nesting selector</code> page to follow the pattern used by other CSS reference docs (e.g. <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Selectors/Next-sibling_combinator\" rel=\"nofollow\">Next-sibling combinator</a>):</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>The <code class=\"notranslate\">## Syntax</code> section is replaced with a concise <code class=\"notranslate\">plain</code> code block showing the three forms of <code class=\"notranslate\">&amp;</code> at a glance (descendant, attached, reversed context)</li>\n<li>The detailed explanations previously living as sub-sections of <code class=\"notranslate\">## Syntax</code> are moved into a new <code class=\"notranslate\">## Description</code> section with three sub-sections: <code class=\"notranslate\">&amp;</code> and whitespace, appending <code class=\"notranslate\">&amp;</code> to reverse context, and <code class=\"notranslate\">&amp;</code> cannot represent pseudo-elements</li>\n<li>The orphaned \"all styles apply to document\" sentence in the outside-nested-rule example is moved above the code blocks where it belongs</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The previous Syntax section was too verbose for a reference page, making it hard to scan the different forms of <code class=\"notranslate\">&amp;</code> at a glance. The detailed explanations are still valuable for first-time learners but belong in a Description section, not Syntax.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #42940.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3862299172\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42940\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/42940/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42940\">#42940</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45288",
            "title": "fix(css): simplify Syntax section for nesting selector (#42940)",
            "date_modified": "2026-08-22T10:14:23.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-08-22T10:12:50.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "BHUVANSH855",
                "url": "https://github.com/BHUVANSH855"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/185269030?u=1fc22565ccf4566b6f734fabaa87e03d9a31cfe4&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Adds an <code class=\"notranslate\">## Examples</code> section to the <code class=\"notranslate\">dir</code> global attribute page with four practical sub-examples covering all three attribute values, and adds the W3C bidi tutorial link to <code class=\"notranslate\">## See also</code>.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The <code class=\"notranslate\">dir</code> attribute page had no examples at all, making it hard for readers to understand when and how to use each value. The new examples show:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>explicit <code class=\"notranslate\">ltr</code>/<code class=\"notranslate\">rtl</code> on paragraphs of different languages</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">dir=\"auto\"</code> for user-generated or unknown-language content</li>\n<li>inline bidirectional text using <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;bdi&gt;</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;bdo&gt;</code></li>\n<li>setting document-level direction on the <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;html&gt;</code> element with per-element overrides</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The W3C bidi tutorial link was also requested in the issue as a useful external reference.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">W3C tutorial linked in See also: <a href=\"https://www.w3.org/International/tutorials/bidi-xhtml/index.en.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://www.w3.org/International/tutorials/bidi-xhtml/index.en.html</a></p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #44052.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4406387165\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44052\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/44052/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44052\">#44052</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45287",
            "title": "html: add examples for the dir global attribute",
            "date_modified": "2026-08-22T09:53:40.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-08-22T09:52:07.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "BHUVANSH855",
                "url": "https://github.com/BHUVANSH855"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55398995?u=9f6a9837c9879eceb0abde487a338b92d4e206fc&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This is long-overdue continuation of <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3523568981\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41569\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/41569/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41569\">#41569</a>. This time, I've added an XML namespaces guide (which fixes two broken links in the \"Anatomy of the DOM\" guide I wrote last time!). It explains the namespace syntax, what's actually lacking in HTML (just the syntax, not the runtime behavior), and summarizes all APIs that interact with namespaces.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I've also fixed the property pages <code class=\"notranslate\">localName</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">prefix</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">namespaceURI</code>, and <code class=\"notranslate\">name</code>/<code class=\"notranslate\">tagName</code> for <code class=\"notranslate\">Element</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">Attr</code>, paying extra attention about when and where HTML performs case normalization, and where the namespace syntax does not work. The examples are now modern (no quirky XHTML markup) and directly runnable.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45284",
            "title": "Modernize DOM guide (3): new XML namespaces guide, fix issues in namespace properties",
            "date_modified": "2026-08-25T21:20:56.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-08-21T18:14:26.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Josh-Cena",
                "url": "https://github.com/Josh-Cena"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105274?u=173310b843e2751843265438af8cfb79eda02039&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Rewrites the existing <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/SVG/Guides/Linking\" rel=\"nofollow\">Linking guide</a> to give an overview of three different ways things can be linked in SVG.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Part of the fill the gaps project</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5019644895\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/mdn/issues/852\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/mdn/issues/852/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/mdn/issues/852\">mdn/mdn#852</a></li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45280",
            "title": "Rewrite the SVG linking guide",
